==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|tolmetsche}}. Compare {{cog|sla-pro|*tъlmačь||interpreter}} (Russian {{m|ru|sc=Cyrl|толма́ч}}, Polish {{m|pl|tłumacz}}), Hungarian {{m|hu|tolmács}}, borrowed from a {{etyl|trk|de}} language, from Proto-Turkic {{m|trk-pro|*tilmaç}} (cf. {{cog|tr|dilmaç||translator, interpreter}}).

